WEBVTT

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.390
These sugar donuts are good.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.500
Indeed!

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.500
Misa-chan, yours looks good, too.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.560
Yeah. I'm going to feed some to the pigeon.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.950
Donuts are so good, I can't stop eating them.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.970
Here. Would you like a mint?

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:18.360
Yeah!

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.000
Thanks.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.540
What a beautiful house.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.480
I bet it's full of memories.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.540
What about you? What are your 
memories of your family like?

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:32.000
Well, I have lots of 
memories of family trips,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.090
but half of them are of arguments.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.130
How about you?

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.550
All I remember is going to 
festivals with my mom and dad.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.180
They bought me cotton candy.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:47.060
So Harajuku's pop icon, cotton candy, 
is part of your memories, too.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.440
Not the colorful ones that are popular 
now, but pure white cotton candy.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.940
I was so happy, I took one 
bite and saved the rest.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.910
But the next day, it had shrunk.
It made me sad.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:02.000
You wanted to keep it forever.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.120
I'm remembering all kinds of things now.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.040
Rito-chan, I love this house, too.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.140
So do I, indeed!

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.550
So do I, of course.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.830
When you all say you love it...

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.180
What?

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.600
Nothing.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:59.420
Are you interested in that jacket?

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:02.950
Firmer fabrics are popular 
right now, so I got some.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.280
Isn't it cute?

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.060
Really? You're my fan? Thanks!

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:09.870
How do you like this new character?

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.850
Wow, a poodle!

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.360
They're always popular. I like it.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.880
Poodles look cute, but they're 
actually hunting dogs.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.390
Maybe it's the gap between 
their appearance and their

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.720
hunter background that makes them popular.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:26.140
Is the design okay?

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.250
Yeah. If you like it, I'm okay with it.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:36.120
Miss, are you looking at your bracelet again?

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.970
You must really like it.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:38.900
Yes, indeed.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.010
I know. We have more beads.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.360
Why don't you try making one?

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.450
Me? Make one?

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:47.660
Yeah.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.600
I don't have to make any.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.240
You'll make them for me, indeed.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.360
Yeah, but...

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.240
You'll have fun making one.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.390
Fun?

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.310
Creating is fun.

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.400
How is it fun?

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:06.470
It feels good when someone 
compliments something you've made.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.620
That customer said she 
was a huge fan of mine.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.200
She complimented my clothes.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.190
You're a famous magazine model.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:19.990
I feel awesomely happy when I get likes 
from my followers on my sweets blog.

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:23.070
I'm sure the likes you get from your 
400,000 followers are great.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:29.810
Yeah. I get more likes when I take photos 
of things that are popular alongside sweets.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:31.780
That extra touch is important.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.990
Just uploading them won't make people look.

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:36.600
I'm particular about when I upload them, too.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:43.470
Midori-chan, is it true that you got foreign 
followers after uploading your illustrations?

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.130
Yeah. Amazing, right?

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:50.430
Next time, I'm thinking about changing the 
style so it'll appeal more to foreigners.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:52.880
You're so skillful.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.190
Yeah. In this world, you can't 
just draw what you want.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.520
Midori-chan, you're so grown-up.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:04.360
Rito, what do you enjoy?

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.570
Oh, me?

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:12.200
I guess... right now, just drawing 
what I feel like drawing.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.220
I think that suits you.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:18.840
Yeah. Draw a lot and publish a lot.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:22.340
Yeah.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:24.340
Rito?

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:26.800
I'm going for a walk.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:32.340
Drawing what I like makes me happy, but...

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.730
Thank you.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:39.570
Welcome, Rito-chan.

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:41.200
What would you like today?

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.750
Got it.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.900
One discussion of your concerns coming up.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.490
You're not confident about your drawings?

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:54.830
Yeah.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:06:00.230
What? But Park gets lots of customers, 
and your popularity is rising.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:06.100
Yeah, but they're fans of Mari's modeling 
or followers of Kotoko's blog.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:09.090
I heard your drawings are 
cute and popular, too.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:10.840
I don't know.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:14.810
No one's ever complimented my 
drawings before, so I'm not sure.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.220
Even though they're so good?

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:20.770
I was too embarrassed to show 
anyone my drawings at school.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.240
My grades in art class were average.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.440
I've never won any awards, either.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.720
Really? That's a surprise.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:32.210
Unlike Mari and Kotoko, 
I don't have fans or followers.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.460
I just draw what I want to draw.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.480
I'm not sure I'll ever become popular.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:45.040
I see. I hope you do.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:47.010
What?

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:51.300
Is that...

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.520
What is that?

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.270
I need to go.

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:58.680
Where are you going?

00:06:58.680 --> 00:06:59.940
It's too dangerous!

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.440
I'll be fine.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:02.530
They're here!

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:03.280
They're here!

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.020
They're here!

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.020
Scoopers are here!

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.400
Found it.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.810
It's slowly flying through the sky.

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:12.780
I hate how this doesn't surprise me anymore.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.640
I'm calling Rito-chan.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:16.030
We're meeting her there?

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:18.880
Then we should change into 
clothes that are easier to spot.

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:19.250
Yeah.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.710
Okay, let's go.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:26.170
Misa-chan, stay here where it's safe.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.630
Okay, indeed.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:33.940
Urahara, deploy.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.450
Rito-chan still isn't here?

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.750
We're in the right place, right?

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:50.080
Sorry I'm late.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.910
It's okay. We just got here.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.160
That's it.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:56.180
I've got it.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:59.500
Wait! We don't know how it'll attack.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:02.790
So we'll say hello first.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:09.960
Huh? Over already?

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:15.370
The thread covered up the hole?

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:18.710
It's making more threads... 
In fact, it's mostly thread now.

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:20.680
Maybe the thread is its actual body.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:22.480
It's coming.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.820
No way! Why me?

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:33.940
Stay away!

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:36.160
Leave me alone!

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:37.570
Why does it keep following Mari?

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:38.960
Because she attacked it?

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.620
If that hurt, I'll apologize!

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:48.710
Let me go!

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:49.320
Mari!

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:57.460
You're okay.

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.470
Thanks.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.560
That was like going on a thrill ride.

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:07.350
Rito-chan, Mari-chan! Watch out!

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:13.320
The threads...

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.320
I can't cut it with this!

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.030
Just don't touch it, right?

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:21.310
Ew, what is this?

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.460
It's making more and more threads.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:26.580
I already have all the sewing thread I need!

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:32.210
It's running?

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.400
Let's go after it.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.220
Kotoko, can you find its weakness?

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.630
Gathering data now.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:42.720
Hey, where are you going?

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.660
Don't tell me you don't have a plan.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:48.440
The creative things around 
here are Rito-chan's drawings.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:51.960
They never learn.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:56.580
But the Scoopers must have pretty 
good taste, to target Rito's drawings.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:57.330
Huh?

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:59.910
Your drawings are cute.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:03.300
The Scoopers want my drawings?

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:08.340
No one's ever complimented 
my drawings before.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.300
Rito-chan, Mari-chan! We've got trouble!

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.430
The Urahara's been dispelled!

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:16.880
What? How?

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:17.760
Could it be...

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:19.600
Rito, what's wrong?

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.600
Look! The Scooper!

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.020
It's after the drawing!

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.020
Urahara, deploy.

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:29.940
The Urahara! But why?

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:30.930
Rito, hurry!

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:31.820
I can't!

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:32.490
Why not?

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:33.410
I don't know.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:34.640
Mari, Kotoko.

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:36.690
Either of you, deploy the Urahara.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.620
Give me a minute.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:39.240
Sorry. We won't make it in time.

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:44.410
Please! Not that drawing!

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.640
It took it...

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:05.000
Target has vanished...

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:11.830
Welcome back, indeed.

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:13.110
Did you defeat it?

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.710
Unfortunately, the answer is no.

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:18.680
It escaped after stealing 
the drawing on the wall.

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:21.560
That's unfortunate, indeed.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:23.340
Sorry, guys.

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:26.660
It's not your fault.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:29.370
No one said the Urahara 
could suddenly revert.

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:34.710
It shouldn't revert until you choose to.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:38.840
What? Rito obviously didn't do it herself.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:42.080
True. Perhaps it's not working correctly.

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:45.380
The manual should've mentioned that.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:49.820
Wait, Mari-chan, don't you push buttons 
without reading the manual first?

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:53.690
Yeah. I throw out the manual 
before the packaging.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.530
Anyway, that thread monster is a handful.

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.980
We have to do something about those threads.

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:02.450
Should we freeze it like last time?

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:05.180
I'll try improving the freezing bombs!

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:07.730
Frozen solid strategy part two, huh?

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:10.910
Even if we defeat it, 
that drawing won't come back.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:16.710
Don't get depressed.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:20.420
Let's create together to 
cheer ourselves up, indeed!

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:21.800
Misa-chan...

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.740
Miss, now isn't the time.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:26.390
Misa-chan, I appreciate the sentiment, but...

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:32.680
Misa-chan, the color and size of 
your beads are all over the place.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:35.900
Perhaps this is too difficult for you.

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:37.840
Misa-chan...

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:42.030
Misa-chan, let me see that.

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:48.620
It'll look pretty if you use beads of the 
same size and colors from the same family.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:50.540
Like this.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.240
Here. Now you try it.

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:56.500
Okay, indeed.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:02.580
That's it.

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:07.140
Now you just hide the knot inside 
the beads, and you're done.

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:13.940
I did it, indeed!

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:17.850
I-I can't believe you 
actually created something.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:19.000
It's cute.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.720
It looks nice, Misa-chan.

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:21.670
Huh?

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.470
The color combination is cute.

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:25.180
It's this year's colors.

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:27.400
It really is cute.

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:31.620
Well? Isn't creating fun?

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:34.610
This... is fun, indeed!

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:35.860
Great.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.080
Maybe I'll recruit you for Park.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:42.380
Everyone... Thank you, indeed.

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:46.510
The threads clearly moved with purpose.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:49.280
There must be a core controlling them.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:55.180
If we can use these improved freezing bombs 
to stop their movements and find the core...

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:02.400
Misa-chan.

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:07.950
I was very happy when you told me 
the ring I made was good, indeed.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.340
You really did a very good job.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.850
Being complimented feels good, doesn't it?

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:18.040
I was really happy when everyone 
complimented that drawing, too.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.540
Compliments make you happy, too?

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.010
Of course.

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:27.510
I've always loved drawing, but...

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:31.390
I used to be happy just 
drawing what I wanted.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:35.740
But over time, I wanted them to please others.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:40.480
That's when I met Mari and Kotoko.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:47.330
When I started working at Park, 
they told me my drawings were cute.

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:50.490
No one had ever told me that before.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:51.570
I was so happy.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:58.620
After talking to them, I learned that 
they wanted to make cute things, too.

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:04.230
So the three of us got permission 
to open a shop over spring break.

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:11.920
Mari and Kotoko taught me what 
I should do and what's popular.

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:15.470
We started getting more customers, 
and I was really happy.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:20.950
Eventually, being asked to 
draw something made me happy.

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:24.400
That's why, in that moment, I...

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.190
What moment? What happened?

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.110
Nothing.

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:29.780
They're here!

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:30.420
They're here!

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:31.030
They're here!

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:32.240
They're here again!

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:38.660
Found it!

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:41.100
I wish our only repeat customers were human.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:41.770
Right, Rito?

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:42.580
Seriously.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.050
Let's go!

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:49.010
Good luck, indeed.

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:52.750
I don't like those threads.

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:54.070
Mari-chan, here.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:55.970
Is this one of those freezing bombs?

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.290
It freezes faster than the previous ones.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:01.230
And these do more than freeze.

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:04.970
Rito-chan, cut away the frozen 
threads and find the core.

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:08.420
If we defeat the core, 
the threads should stop.

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:09.180
Got it.

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:10.160
I'll look for it.

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.080
You won't get away this time.

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:14.990
No way! Can it hear me?

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:18.080
Mari-chan, shoot!

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.200
I'd like to, but I can't!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.450
Lock on!

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:23.190
It's not giving me time to!

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:26.180
Could you ask it to hold still for a minute?

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:27.920
Does it understand Japanese?

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:29.840
Just so you know, I was joking.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.570
I'm joking, too.

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:32.820
Mari, try to get away.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:33.760
I'll give it a shot.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:39.590
Wow. Rito-chan, you're amazing!

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:41.520
Maybe I'll ask you to cut 
some fabrics next time.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.140
Mari, now.

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:44.070
Okay.

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:46.600
This'll be cold. Think you can handle it?

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:48.860
It's -40 degrees!

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:54.220
It ate it?

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:55.110
You can't be serious!

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:58.660
No one told me their movements 
would be so controlled!

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:00.490
You want some more, then?

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.490
No way! I'm out?

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.000
Kotoko, what should we do?

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.230
Um... We need to find the core.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:13.860
To do that, we need to stop 
the threads' movements.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.690
To stop the threads, 
we need to find the core...

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:18.180
Kotoko, calm down.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:21.430
I need to start over with gathering data.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:23.090
You're joking, right?

00:17:23.090 --> 00:17:24.840
It's not a joke!

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:27.440
I wish it were!

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:29.830
Mari!

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:36.820
I can't move.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.600
Rito-chan, Mari-chan!

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:39.970
Kotoko, run!

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:41.240
I can't!

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.340
Don't force yourself to fight!

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:43.080
Run!

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.370
But...

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:46.900
Kotoko!

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:47.820
I'm sorry.

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.480
I can't believe it caught all of us.

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:53.130
I knew we were close friends, but <i>this</i> close?

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.380
Electricity?

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:06.490
What should we do?

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:08.120
It's back to normal.

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:10.220
I feel... weak...

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:11.610
What's going on?

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:14.360
What? Where is it going?

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:17.080
I'd appreciate it if it'd take us to Park!

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:19.120
It doesn't look like it is.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:20.030
This direction...

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:25.700
It's after that drawing.

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:27.130
That house...

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:28.450
Is something wrong?

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:29.220
Huh?

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:31.670
Nothing, indeed.

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:35.230
Are they all right?

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:37.560
They should be awakening soon.

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:38.880
It should be fine.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:43.100
Really? I'm looking forward to it, indeed.

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:47.540
By the way, does the 
Amatsumara ever malfunction?

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:48.560
I don't think it's possible.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:55.150
Here again?

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:57.220
What else is here?

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:04.520
Not that house!

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:06.710
Why can't we deploy the Urahara?

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:08.540
The Amatsumara isn't responding.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:11.500
It's my fault.

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:13.040
Rito?

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:18.210
When I knew the Scoopers wanted 
my drawing, I hesitated.

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:21.590
But I never asked for it to be stolen!

00:19:22.190 --> 00:19:24.410
Rito, what are you talking about?

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:27.190
Look! Rito-chan's house is disappearing!

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:32.480
Dad, Mom, where are you?

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:36.470
No, Grandma! Don't take me away!

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:38.130
This is my house!

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:40.200
No! I'm going home!

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:41.760
Stop!

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:43.460
Rito?

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.340
You've taken enough already.

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:49.120
You want to take even more from me?

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:57.650
I won't let you take my house!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.000
Rito-chan!

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:11.870
Rito!

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.230
Wait, Rito-chan!

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:15.820
We'll go with you.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.650
Give it back!

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.270
Rito!

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:25.740
Stop! Don't eat her!

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:55.440
What is this?

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.090
Kotoko, your body...

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:58.340
And yours.

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:00.880
No, not the face!

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:02.030
What's going on?

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.240
Why are we suddenly...

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:08.320
Maybe it's not sudden.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:10.040
What do you mean?

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:13.530
Remember the marks I told you about?

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:17.600
Maybe our bodies were already 
beginning to change back then.

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:19.350
Wait a minute!

00:21:19.350 --> 00:21:21.670
You examined us and didn't 
find anything wrong.

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:24.160
I didn't find anything.

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:28.010
But I should've kept looking.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:29.100
I'm sorry.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:34.280
Sorry. I didn't mean to blame you.

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:36.840
But what's going to happen to us?

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:42.570
Misa-chan...

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:45.910
You don't need to hide it, indeed.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:50.530
You're not human anymore, indeed!

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:51.760
What?

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:28.470
Misa-sama, apparently this is 
a food known as sakuramochi.

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:29.780
What does it taste like?

00:23:29.780 --> 00:23:30.960
I hear it's sweet and sour.

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:32.000
Which is it?

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:33.330
Uh, sweet and so—

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:34.560
Which is it?

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:35.420
Uh, um—

00:23:35.420 --> 00:23:37.010
Which is it?
